{title: Saved by Grace}
{artist: Fanny J. Crosby / George C. Stebbins}
{genre: Gospel}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Closing}
{key: F}
{tempo: 80}
{time: 4/4}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]Some day the silver [Bb]cord will [F]break
And I no [C7]more as now shall [F]sing
But [F]oh, the joy when [Bb]I shall [F]wake
With[C7]in the palace of the [F]King
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
And I shall [F]see Him face to [Bb]face
And [F]tell the story [C7]Saved by [F]grace
And I shall [F]see Him face to [Bb]face
And [F]tell the story [C7]Saved by [F]grace
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]Some day my earthly [Bb]house will [F]fall
I can[C7]not tell how soon 'twill [F]be
But [F]this I know, my [Bb]All in [F]All
Has [C7]now a place in heaven for [F]me
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]Some day, when fades the [Bb]golden [F]sun
Be[C7]neath the rosy-tinted [F]west
My [F]blessed Lord shall [Bb]say, "Well [F]done"
And [C7]I shall enter into [F]rest
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[F]Some day: till then I'll [Bb]watch and [F]wait
My [C7]lamp all trimmed and burning [F]bright
That [F]when my Saviour [Bb]opens the [F]gate
My [C7]soul to Him may take its [F]flight
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
